    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a30">

                <pb facs="0290" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg218"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 29 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tinsley to Mr. Barrows</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 29,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received the inclosed letter this morning
                    and soon after called upon the writer at the county jail. I had an interview
                    with him, and he requested me to forward his certificate of naturalization as an
                    American citizen to the United States minister at London, and to request
                    respectfully his excellency’s interference in his behalf.</p>
                <p>I send inclosed his letter and certificate that you may take such action in the
                    matter as you may deem proper.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN R. TINSLEY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consular
                        Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
